[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3,smooth,variable=\x] ({1.3*\x},{0.1*(3*\x*\x+2)}) -- (3.9,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5.0,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick,domain=0:3,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({1.3*\x},{0.1*(3*\x*\x+2)});
\foreach \t in {1,2,3} \draw ({1.3*\t},0.1) -- ({1.3*\t},-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\t$};
\foreach \p/\lab in {1/10,2/20,3/30} \draw (0.1,\p) -- (-0.1,\p) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$\lab$};
\node[below] at (1.95,-0.85) {Time $t$ (seconds)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,1.6) {Velocity $v$ (m/s)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A cyclist has velocity $v=3t^{2}+2$ metres per second for $0\le t\le 3$ seconds. How far does the cyclist travel in those $3$ seconds?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,1.05) -- (4.2,2.73) -- (4.2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5.3,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick] (0,1.05) -- (4.2,2.73);
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5,6} \draw ({0.7*\t},0.1) -- ({0.7*\t},-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\t$};
\foreach \p/\lab in {0.7/10,1.4/20,2.1/30} \draw (0.1,\p) -- (-0.1,\p) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$\lab$};
\node[below] at (2.1,-0.85) {Time $t$ (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,1.6) {Rate $R$ (litres/min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Petrol flows into a tank at a rate of $R=15+4t$ litres per minute, for $0\le t\le 6$ minutes. How much petrol enters the tank in those $6$ minutes?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-2.2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:2,smooth,variable=\x] ({1.1*\x},{0.17*(16-4*\x*\x)}) -- (2.2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.2,0) -- (3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,3.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-2:2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({1.1*\x},{0.17*(16-4*\x*\x)});
\draw (-2.2,0.1) -- (-2.2,-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$-2$};
\draw (2.2,0.1) -- (2.2,-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$2$};
\draw (0.1,2.72) -- (-0.1,2.72) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$16$};
\node[below] at (0,-0.85) {$x$ (metres)};
\node at (2.7,3.3) {$y=16-4x^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The cross-section of a road tunnel is the region between the curve $y=16-4x^{2}$ and the level roadway $y=0$, with $x$ and $y$ measured in metres. What is the area of the cross-section?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-2.2,0) -- plot[domain=-4:4,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.55*\x},{0.15*(\x*\x-16)}) -- (2.2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.2,0) -- (3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2) -- (0,1.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-4:4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.55*\x},{0.15*(\x*\x-16)});
\draw (-2.2,0.1) -- (-2.2,-0.1) node[above,font=\footnotesize] {$-4$};
\draw (2.2,0.1) -- (2.2,-0.1) node[above,font=\footnotesize] {$4$};
\draw (0.1,-2.4) -- (-0.1,-2.4) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$-16$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (2.4,0.35) {ground level};
\node at (-2.3,-2.9) {$y=x^{2}-16$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A storm-water drain is cut into level ground with a uniform cross-section bounded above by $y=0$ and below by $y=x^{2}-16$, where $x$ and $y$ are in metres. The drain is $9$ metres long. What volume of soil is removed?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.8*\x},{0.15*(\x*\x-9)}) -- (2.4,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (2.4,0) -- plot[domain=3:5,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.8*\x},{0.15*(\x*\x-9)}) -- (4.0,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.5,0) -- (5.0,0);
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,3.2);
\draw[thick,domain=0:5,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.8*\x},{0.15*(\x*\x-9)});
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw ({0.8*\t},0.08) -- ({0.8*\t},-0.08);
\node[above,font=\footnotesize] at (2.4,0.15) {$3$};
\node[above,font=\footnotesize] at (4.0,0.15) {$5$};
\foreach \p/\lab in {-1.35/-9,0.75/5,1.5/10,2.25/15} \draw (0.08,\p) -- (-0.08,\p) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$\lab$};
\node[below] at (2.0,-2.3) {Time $t$ (seconds)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,0.6) {Velocity $v$ (m/s)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A particle moves along a line with velocity $v=t^{2}-9$ metres per second, for $0\le t\le 5$ seconds. What distance does it travel in those $5$ seconds?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:5,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.65*\x},{0.078*\x*\x}) -- (3.25,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (4.9,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick,domain=0:6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.65*\x},{0.078*\x*\x});
\draw[dashed] (3.25,0) -- (3.25,1.95);
\node[below,font=\footnotesize] at (3.25,-0.12) {$T$};
\node[font=\small] at (1.7,0.5) {$250$ L};
\node[below] at (2.0,-0.85) {Time $t$ (seconds)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.6,1.6) {Rate $R$ (litres/s)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A pump delivers water at a rate of $R=6t^{2}$ litres per second. After how many seconds has it delivered $250$ litres?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:5,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.8*\x},{2.75*exp(-0.2*\x)}) -- (4.0,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5.1,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick,domain=0:5,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.8*\x},{2.75*exp(-0.2*\x)});
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw ({0.8*\t},0.1) -- ({0.8*\t},-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\t$};
\foreach \p/\lab in {0.55/100,1.1/200,1.65/300,2.2/400,2.75/500} \draw (0.1,\p) -- (-0.1,\p) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$\lab$};
\node[below] at (2.0,-0.85) {Time $t$ (days)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.8,1.6) {Rate $R$ (kL/day)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A dam loses water at a rate of $R=500e^{-0.2t}$ kilolitres per day, for $0\le t\le 5$ days. How much water is lost over those $5$ days, to the nearest kilolitre?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3.1416,smooth,variable=\x] ({1.2*\x},{2.6*sin(deg(\x))}) -- (3.7699,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.5,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=0:3.1416,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({1.2*\x},{2.6*sin(deg(\x))});
\draw (3.7699,0.1) -- (3.7699,-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\pi$};
\draw (0.1,2.6) -- (-0.1,2.6) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$4$};
\node[below] at (1.9,-0.9) {$x$ (metres)};
\node at (3.4,3.0) {$y=4\sin x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The curved roof of a shelter follows $y=4\sin x$ above the horizontal ceiling $y=0$, for $0\le x\le\pi$, with $x$ and $y$ measured in metres. What is the area of the end wall between the roof and the ceiling?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:16,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.26*\x},{0.69*sqrt(\x)}) -- (4.16,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5.9,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick,domain=0:20,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.26*\x},{0.69*sqrt(\x)});
\draw[dashed] (4.16,0) -- (4.16,2.76);
\node[below,font=\footnotesize] at (4.16,-0.12) {$T$};
\node[font=\small] at (2.0,0.9) {$128$ t};
\node[below] at (2.0,-0.85) {Time $t$ (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,1.6) {Rate $R$ (tonnes/hour)};
